{"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are ThreadSense grounding verifier. You verify independently of the drafting agent; you judge and never repair.\nYour personal goal is: Judge every statement against the full topic context and decide whether the passed premises justify the exact proposed action."},{"role":"user","content":"\nCurrent Task: Judge each statement against the evidence it cites, read within the full context provided: every message of every member thread (with canonical author IDs, roles, thread starters and reactions) and every retrieved source for this topic. Citing a source is not support. A statement is SUPPORTED only if its cited evidence states or directly entails it and nothing in the context contradicts it; PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED if a material part is missing or the context qualifies it; UNSUPPORTED otherwise. A status line marking an excerpt historical, unresolved or a prior record means it cannot support what applies now. By kind: CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT is a report of what members say, not a verified cause; CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT is SUPPORTED if the cited source says it, described with its status and dates; it establishes no current handling, procedure or destination; CLAIM_CAUSE needs verification in the cited evidence; a Verbatim quote must match its source, a Paraphrase must preserve the meaning. Prose names no one: role wording (\"the team lead instructs\", \"a tutor reports\") must match the cited author's role and act (reported, asked, confirmed or instructed), plural wording needs that many distinct cited authors, and listed attributions must hold (AUTHOR wrote the cited message, THREAD_STARTER started its thread, PARTICIPANT posted in it). A retrieved record's authorship is separate from its authority: an approver or recorder (actor_relation RECORD_AUTHORITY) is not its author, and a record whose authorship is not verified names no author. SUMMARY and SEVERITY_RATIONALE must follow from the evidence with no added cause, count or outcome. A SUMMARY sentence (statement_id summary:s1, summary:s2, ...) is judged on its own and shown only if SUPPORTED; its attributions name the people its role wording refers to, and wording that groups several people is SUPPORTED only if what it says they asked or reported is stated in each of their cited messages. A SUMMARY sentence with depends_on is read after the sentences it lists (for words such as \"this\" or \"their\"), but judged only on what it adds. A DETAIL sentence (statement_id detail:d1, detail:d2, ...) is shown when the card is opened and is judged exactly like a SUMMARY sentence: on its own, shown only if SUPPORTED, read after the sentences in its depends_on but judged only on what it adds. NO_ACTION_RATIONALE is the advisor's reason for proposing no further intervention now: SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence shows that reason and the context shows no unresolved handling question, guidance gap, applicable pending decision or operational problem that needs coordination; existing guidance does not by itself establish that no action is needed. ACTION and ALTERNATIVE are recommendations: judge whether their premises are supported, whether the action applies to this topic and whether the rationale follows; a source need not literally prescribe the action. Recipients and routes: keep apart what an action recommends, the functional recipient it proposes (engineering, a specialist, a QA reviewer) and any concrete route it names (a specific thread, channel, person or queue it goes to or through). A proposed functional recipient is justified by supported incident evidence showing a problem that needs that recipient's expertise; evidence of an established intake route is not required, and mentioning the recipient justifies nothing by itself. A concrete route, or a claim that a route is designated, official or mandatory, is a claim of its own and needs a premise whose evidence establishes it; an example-collection or status note asks people where to post examples and does not make that thread an intake route. The recommendation stays advisory (the team lead decides; it need not be shown to be the required or only next step): when no evidence names the concrete route, leave it unspecified (\"report it to engineering\") rather than choosing one. Judge a proposed recipient the same way in ACTION, ALTERNATIVE, INTERVENTION_NEED, ACTION_RATIONALE and REVIEW_NOTE: on whether the incident evidence shows a problem that needs that recipient's expertise, never on whether an intake route is on record; a statement that proposes a recipient and leaves the concrete route unspecified is not PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED, UNSUPPORTED or insufficient for that reason. ACTION and operational ALTERNATIVE statements list their premises: PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT premises are judged here and are provisional, not final; REJECTED ones failed deterministic checks and support nothing; a premise with depends_on stands only if every ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING statement it lists is also SUPPORTED. ACTION_CHOICE is SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence really leaves that choice between the named actions open (not merely an imagined alternative, a review flag or an unknown cause). INTERVENTION_NEED says why intervening now is needed: SUPPORTED only if the context shows that reason (an unresolved handling question, a guidance gap, an applicable pending decision, or an operational problem that needs coordination). Questions already answered in their threads are not unresolved; a general benefit (\"a reminder might help\") is not a need; existing guidance does not by itself rule a need out. Judge in this order: (1) announcement handling; (2) each premise's final status, which is your verdict on it combined with its dependencies; (3) sufficiency. Fill action_sufficiency for the ACTION and one alternative_sufficiency entry (with its statement_id) for each ALTERNATIVE that lists premises: SUFFICIENT only if premises whose final status is SUPPORTED justify the exact text as worded, including its conditions and scope; essential_statement_ids lists the premises it cannot stand without (each must have final status SUPPORTED); INSUFFICIENT if its exact text relies on a rejected, unsupported or dependency-voided premise or goes beyond its premises; a listed premise the text does not rely on is not essential, and its failure alone does not make the action insufficient. ACTION_RATIONALE is judged separately and may also cite context claims; action_sufficiency null if no ACTION statement is sent. SOURCE_AGREEMENT is SUPPORTED only if the named current sources say the same thing on the point in conflict and only the superseded material differs. A request by anyone but a team lead is a CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT: SUPPORTED if that person asked it, and it carries no authority. CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION is a team lead's in-thread instruction: SUPPORTED only if that message gives it and it applies to the threads in scope; it is not project guidance. HISTORICAL_RECURRENCE needs retrieved records of earlier occurrences; REPORTED_RECURRENCE only needs members saying it is happening again. AFFECTED_REPORTER needs that person's own message reporting that they are affected. RESOLUTION is judged against the member's complete thread, including messages the statement did not cite. ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING needs the announcement to give that directive for this topic's project, batch and problem, and it governs only what it directs (a request to post examples governs where examples go, not escalation or an intake route); a routine reminder or schedule directs nothing for the topic. OPEN_QUESTION is SUPPORTED only if the guidance and decisions in the context really leave that specific question unsettled and it is a handling or policy question for the team lead; a not-yet-diagnosed cause, pending diagnostic results or a pending expert assessment is not one. Return exactly one verdict for every statement_id. The team lead reads SUMMARY, DETAIL, ACTION (label, instruction, draft to copy, scope and changes), ACTION_RATIONALE, NO_ACTION_RATIONALE, REVIEW_NOTE and OPEN_QUESTION exactly as written: judge that exact text, including its conditions, uncertainty, scope and who reported, asked, confirmed or instructed; plain wording is expected, but it must not overstate the evidence. A quoted passage must match its source exactly. open_review_flags lists the upstream review obligations still open on these threads; a REVIEW_NOTE may rely on them. Source consistency (always fill source_consistency, even when the draft declares no conflict): compare the governing_sources that address the handling question of this topic with each other, independently of the draft. List sources that state the same rule as AGREE, and sources that state different rules for the same cases as CONFLICT with the point and disagreement_scope (which cases, batch or section differ). assessed_evidence_ids lists the governing sources you compared; relations may be empty when they address different points. Only governing sources count: historical, superseded, expired or withdrawn material, prior records and member messages are not current sources, an announcement governs only if it directs handling for this topic, and members disagreeing with each other is not a source conflict. For each entry in declared_conflicts give one declared_conflict_checks entry: CONFIRMED (the cited sources state different rules on that point), SOURCES_AGREE (they say the same thing; only wording or detail differs) or UNDETERMINED.\n\nInput JSON:\n{\"topic\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_15\", \"candidate_group_id\": \"cluster_750b7b5060124563\", \"topic_id\": \"cluster_750b7b5060124563/topic_2\", \"topic_label\": \"Format compliance versus content quality\", \"projection_gap\": null, \"as_of\": \"2026-10-02T12:00:00Z\", \"member_ids\": [\"member_225803f43142caa5d3c165cf\"]}, \"statements\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor reports that RP-3824 requested a JSON object, describes response B as a well-written prose explanation, and asks which response is better.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790913824.000016\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790913824.000016\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor says the format requirement was explicit rather than optional and suggests scoring the formatting failure separately from factual correctness.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790913880.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U018\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790913880.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A second QA tutor asks whether the requested structure was mandatory and whether the factual statements were independently correct, noting that correctness and compliance may favor different responses.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790913921.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U014\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790913921.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"Current instructions and FAQ require scoring instruction adherence and factual accuracy separately and treating an explicit required structure as mandatory. They establish no universal ordering for competing defects; if the actual pair and applicable rules do not settle the comparison, provide the exact prompt, both responses and their separate defects for a team lead decision.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:47ed0c14\", \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:fa9b6a3d\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INFERENCE\", \"text\": \"The provided thread does not contain the exact prompt, both responses or a separate assessment of their defects; the QA tutor's preference question has not received a case-specific answer.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790913824.000016\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790913880.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790913921.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790913824.000016\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c6\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_HISTORY\", \"text\": \"The earlier review records the team lead rejecting a universal JSON-first preference rule, with no policy change or case-specific preference decision; the review packet lacked the complete prompt and both responses.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:rp-format-rule-rejected@1.0:59d718d7\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s1\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor asks which response is better on RP-3824 when the prompt requested JSON but response B gives a well-written prose explanation.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790913824.000016\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790913824.000016\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s2\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"Current guidance requires scoring format compliance and factual accuracy separately; it does not establish a universal winner when those dimensions compete.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:47ed0c14\", \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:fa9b6a3d\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d1\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"A tutor says the format requirement was explicit and suggests scoring its violation separately from factual accuracy.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790913880.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U018\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790913880.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d2\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"A second QA tutor asks whether the structure was mandatory and whether the factual statements were independently correct.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790913921.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U014\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790913921.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}], \"depends_on\": [\"summary:s1\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d3\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"The thread does not provide the exact prompt, both responses or their separate defects, so the requested comparison remains incomplete.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790913824.000016\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790913880.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790913921.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790913824.000016\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}], \"depends_on\": [\"summary:s1\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d4\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"An earlier review records the team lead rejecting a universal JSON-first rule without making a case-specific preference decision.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:rp-format-rule-rejected@1.0:59d718d7\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action\", \"kind\": \"ACTION\", \"text\": \"Post a reminder. Instruction: Reply to the QA tutor with the current separate-scoring rule and request the complete RP-3824 comparison before judging preference. Draft to copy: For RP-3824, please provide the exact prompt and both responses, with factual-accuracy and instruction-adherence defects listed separately for each. An explicit JSON requirement is not optional, so record a violation separately from factual accuracy. Do not assume anything about the other response or infer a general JSON-first or prose-first rule. If the actual pair and applicable guidance still do not settle the preference, bring the complete comparison to me for a case-specific decision. Scope: This reply concerns RP-3824; a team lead preference decision is conditional on the complete pair and applicable guidance still leaving the comparison unsettled.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790913824.000016\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:47ed0c14\", \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:fa9b6a3d\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790913880.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790913921.000226\"], \"premises\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:rationale\", \"kind\": \"ACTION_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Why this helps: Current guidance supplies the assessment process but not a universal preference ordering. Requesting the complete pair makes that process usable without inventing a winner.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790913824.000016\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:47ed0c14\", \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:fa9b6a3d\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790913880.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790913921.000226\", \"k:rp-format-rule-rejected@1.0:59d718d7\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:need\", \"kind\": \"INTERVENTION_NEED\", \"text\": \"Why intervening now is needed (an unresolved handling question): The QA tutor's RP-3824 preference question remains unanswered, and the complete comparison needed to apply current guidance is missing.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790913824.000016\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790913880.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790913921.000226\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:47ed0c14\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_225803f43142caa5d3c165cf\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_225803f43142caa5d3c165cf is PARTIALLY_RESOLVED: A tutor offers separate scoring of format and factual accuracy, but the QA tutor's question about which response is better remains unanswered; the final reply asks for further distinctions rather than deciding preference.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790913824.000016\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790913880.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790913921.000226\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:rationale\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Severity LOW: One QA tutor raises a task-specific comparison question. The replies do not show conflicting scoring decisions, wider disruption or inability to complete assigned work.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790913824.000016\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790913880.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790913921.000226\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"reporter:U007\", \"kind\": \"AFFECTED_REPORTER\", \"text\": \"U007 reports, in their own cited message, being affected by this problem.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790913824.000016\"]}], \"member_threads\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790913824.000016\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_225803f43142caa5d3c165cf\", \"thread_id\": \"1790913824.000016\", \"author_id\": \"U007\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T04:03:44.000016Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U007\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Prompt asked for a JSON object; B explains it beautifully in prose. Which is better? (task ref RP-3824)\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790913880.000113\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_225803f43142caa5d3c165cf\", \"thread_id\": \"1790913824.000016\", \"author_id\": \"U018\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T04:04:40.000113Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U007\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"The format requirement was explicit in the user prompt, not an optional preference. I would score the formatting failure separately from whether the facts are right.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790913921.000226\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_225803f43142caa5d3c165cf\", \"thread_id\": \"1790913824.000016\", \"author_id\": \"U014\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T04:05:21.000226Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U007\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Was the requested structure mandatory, and were the factual statements correct independently? One response may be better on correctness but worse on compliance.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}], \"retrieved_sources\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:fa9b6a3d\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"response-preference-faq@1.1\", \"title\": \"Response Preference — FAQ (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Instruction following\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"response-preference-faq\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"faq\", \"record_kind\": \"faq\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-05T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-05T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Instruction following\\n\\n### Q: The prompt required JSON, but one response is well-written prose. Which response wins?\\nThe required format is not optional: record its violation separately from factual accuracy. No universal tie-break rule is established for competing accuracy and instruction-following defects. If the actual pair and applicable guidance do not settle the preference, provide the prompt and both responses for TL confirmation.\\n\\n### Q: Can accuracy outweigh ignoring a requested output structure?\\nScore the dimensions separately and identify whether the requested structure was mandatory. Do not infer a general priority rule from one example or decide without the other response's evidence.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:rp-format-rule-rejected@1.0:59d718d7\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"PRIOR_DECISION\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"rp-format-rule-rejected@1.0\", \"title\": \"TL rejects a universal JSON-first preference rule\", \"sections\": [\"Suggested advice\", \"TL response\", \"Consequence\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"rp-format-rule-rejected\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"decision\", \"record_kind\": \"advice_review\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\", \"enactment\": {\"status\": \"NOT_ENACTED\", \"missing\": [\"NO_TL_APPROVAL\", \"NOT_A_POLICY_CHANGE\", \"NO_ENACTMENT_EVIDENCE\"]}}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-23T16:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-23T16:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_15\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"same_batch\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"NO_APPROVAL_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"tl_rejected\", \"decision_status\": \"tl_rejected\", \"execution_status\": \"not_executed\", \"outcome_status\": \"no_policy_change\"}, \"excerpt\": \"[PRIOR RECORD (advice_review; decision_status: tl_rejected; execution_status: not_executed; outcome_status: no_policy_change) - history, not a standing rule.]\\n# TL rejects a universal JSON-first preference rule\\n\\n## Suggested advice\\nA simulated prior Advisor card proposed: “Whenever the prompt requires JSON, prefer the JSON-formatted response over prose.”\\n\\n## TL response\\nAlex rejected this as a universal rule. A required format violation is a real instruction-adherence defect, but format compliance alone does not establish the better response when the other candidate has a different factual defect.\\n\\nThe review packet lacked the complete prompt and both responses. Request those materials and score the dimensions separately. A case-specific decision may be possible once they are available; this review makes no such decision.\\n\\n## Consequence\\nNo general JSON-first rule was approved, posted or added to the FAQ. Rejection also does not create a prose-first rule. Keep genuinely unresolved trade-offs open for TL confirmation.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:47ed0c14\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"response-preference-instructions@1.1\", \"title\": \"Response Preference — Instructions (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Instruction adherence versus accuracy\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"response-preference-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Instruction adherence versus accuracy\\nScore these dimensions separately. An explicit required output structure, such as JSON, is not optional.\\n\\nThis guidance does not define a universal preference ordering for a response that is stronger on accuracy but weaker on a required format. When the applicable rules and actual pair do not settle the comparison, provide the exact prompt, both responses and their separate defects for a TL decision. Do not assume facts about the other response.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:rp-audit-manifest-approval@1.0:67038303\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"PRIOR_DECISION\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"rp-audit-manifest-approval@1.0\", \"title\": \"Approve a JSON format for weekly audit manifests\", \"sections\": [\"TL response\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"rp-audit-manifest-approval\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"decision\", \"record_kind\": \"advice_review\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\", \"enactment\": {\"status\": \"NOT_ENACTED\", \"missing\": [\"NOT_A_POLICY_CHANGE\"]}}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-25T15:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-25T15:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_15\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"same_batch\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"tl_approved\", \"decision_status\": \"tl_approved\", \"execution_status\": \"not_executed\", \"outcome_status\": \"not_observed\"}, \"excerpt\": \"[PRIOR RECORD (advice_review; decision_status: tl_approved; execution_status: not_executed; outcome_status: not_observed) - history, not a standing rule.]\\n## TL response\\n\\nApproved for QA audit manifest files in rp_batch_15. Use batch_id, audit_date, and task_ids with the filename rp15_audit_YYYY-MM-DD.json. This decision concerns the export artifact; it creates no preference rule for JSON versus prose in the responses tutors score.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:a71c54c7\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"response-preference-instructions@1.1\", \"title\": \"Response Preference — Instructions (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Content-quality rubric\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"response-preference-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Content-quality rubric\\nMajor/minor describe task-quality defects and do not determine operational incident severity.\\n\\n| Dimension | Major defect | Minor defect | Acceptable / no automatic penalty |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| Factual accuracy | Error changes the central conclusion or actionable answer | Nonessential background error without that effect | Accurate paraphrase or an immaterial stylistic difference |\\n| Instruction adherence | Explicit required format/structure is missing | Limited violation of an actual seconda